  "source": {
    "plan": "Callboard row 2026-11-25 (storyhowto, nobody-brings, paper), the earliest planned row on 2026-11-20; Nobody Brings #2, a Milo episode, hook 'Stop bringing Ophelia.' spoken first and big on screen from frame 0, Ghost Light only, about 25s",
    "project": "ppvqmbzuqvzpiuqaiqfy",
    "sql": "select m.*, p.* from monologues m join plays p on p.id=m.play_id where p.copyright_status='public_domain' and m.character_gender ilike 'f%' and m.estimated_duration_seconds between 35 and 60 and coalesce(m.overdone_score,0)<=0.05 and p.author not ilike '%shakespeare%' (then the pieces the app's own search returned were checked by id)",
    "checked": "2026-11-20: monologue 40303 Louisa, 'Where can he be now?' (Love and Intrigue: A Tragedy, Friedrich Schiller, 1784, play 2852, public_domain, Gutenberg 6784), 59 seconds, 109 words, overdone_score 0. The two cards under it are public domain too: Lady H (Martha; or, The Fair at Richmond, play 2970) and Lalain (The Goddess of Reason, Mary Johnston, play 3258)",
    "changed_from_plan": "the row's search, 'dramatic, woman, under a minute, not Shakespeare', returns Katherine, Lady Macbeth and Miranda first in the app (the search does not read 'not Shakespeare'), so the film types a description that does bring a non Shakespeare piece up first: 'a poor girl in love with a nobleman, under a minute' (Louisa first, marked best pick). The why-it-works line is 'heartbroken like Ophelia, and almost nobody brings her' (overdone 0)",
    "app": "Ghost Light web preview built from actorrise main apps/mobile (9da05c7) plus web-preview.patch, dark theme, demo account, 2026-11-20",
    "flow": "flows/search-stop-bringing-ophelia.json (shots -> public/story/2026-11-25-stop-bringing-ophelia/*.png): Book, Search, the typed description, 30 monologues with Louisa first, her page",
    "sticky_note": "Tonight's speech on the search screen showed a line of a copyrighted play (Read It Now!, play 3437), which may not be filmed; a drawn sticky note ('not Ophelia') sits over that card. Nothing on the screen is mocked",
    "voice": "George, one take at stability 0.5, Scribe 0.99, sped up 1.25x with fit_take.py; AI voice, labelled on every platform",
    "new_scene_types": "ophelias (an audition lobby where five actors hold the same OPHELIA page, flowers in their hair, Milo in the middle) with three beats: hook, five (each one's bubble pops with 'O, what a noble mind', counted 1 to 5), snag (he backs away, the scarf is caught on a folding chair, the tote tips over, the phone comes up)",
    "motifs": "milo-among-five-ophelias,ophelia-pages-flowers-in-hair,same-line-bubbles-counted,backs-away-scarf-caught-on-folding-chair,tote-spills,sticky-note-not-ophelia",
